WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.976
A model router selects an endpoint using task type, data sensitivity, model capability, latency target, availability, and cost.

00:00:07.976 --> 00:00:13.089
The eligible set should be determined by policy before performance ranking.

00:00:13.089 --> 00:00:21.066
A cloud model that would answer best is not eligible if the prompt contains data that cannot leave.

00:00:21.066 --> 00:00:26.179
Record the route and policy result so behavior can be explained.

00:00:26.179 --> 00:00:36.610
Local servers and cloud endpoints may expose similar APIs, but details differ across streaming, tool calls, context limits, embeddings, error codes, and safety behavior.

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:41.723
Normalize only the features the application uses and test each route.

00:00:41.723 --> 00:00:47.245
Model outputs are not interchangeable, so fallback may change quality or format.

00:00:47.245 --> 00:00:51.131
Clients need clear expectations when service is degraded.

00:00:51.131 --> 00:00:57.880
Apply rate limits, timeouts, queues, and concurrency controls separately for local capacity and paid endpoints.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:05.856
A local queue should not silently overflow into an expensive cloud route without a cost and privacy decision.

00:01:05.856 --> 00:01:11.787
Fallback logic must distinguish capacity failure, authentication failure, policy denial, and provider outage.

00:01:11.787 --> 00:01:16.491
Some failures should stop the request instead of rerouting it.

00:01:16.491 --> 00:01:22.423
Protect endpoint credentials and keep them out of prompts, client code, and logs.

00:01:22.423 --> 00:01:28.354
Avoid orchestration that copies entire conversations to every candidate model before selecting one.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:33.467
Start with explicit routing rules and a small number of endpoints.

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:38.171
Add automation only when monitoring shows a recurring placement need.

00:01:38.171 --> 00:01:45.738
Good orchestration makes data movement, cost, and failure visible rather than hiding complexity behind one chat box.
